          %h2#details Details
          %p
            First we consider the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in algebras over an ordinary Lawvere theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#OverOrdinaryLawvereTheories"} For algebras over ordinary Lawvere theories
          %p Then we generalize to the case that the Lawvere theory itself is simplicial:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ForAlgebrasOverSimplicialLawvereTheories"} For algebras over simplicial Lawvere theories
          %h3#OverOrdinaryLawvereTheories For algebras over ordinary Lawvere theories
          %p
            Recall that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C^{op})
            itself is modeled by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∘
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C^{op})
                  \\simeq
                  [C, sSet]^\circ
                  \\,,
          %p
            where we regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            and have on the right the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            with the projective or injective model structure, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\circ
            denoting the full enriched subcategory on fibrant-cofibrant objects.
          %p
            This says in particular that every weak
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to \infty \mathrm{Grp}
            is equivalent to a
            %em rectified
            one
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
